INT. RESTAURANT KITCHEN, AFTER CLOSE - NIGHT

Steel counters. A hose coiled on the drain. Five people sit on overturned crates sharing a bottle.

CHEF IMANI JOSEPH, 40s, still in whites. SOUS-CHEF DARIUS PELL, 30s. DISHWASHER PEARL, 50s. WAITER ANSELM, 20s. And a STRANGER in a gray coat, fifties, who wandered in through the alley door.

Imani pours a round. Darius passes the bread. Pearl hums. Anselm laughs. The Stranger accepts a glass and says nothing.

IMANI
So what do we call him?

DARIUS
He's a health inspector.

PEARL
He's not an inspector.

ANSELM
He's a ghost.

DARIUS
(over Anselm)
He ate the last of the soup.

PEARL
(over Darius)
Hush, let the man speak.

STRANGER
Leopold.

IMANI
Leopold what?

LEOPOLD
Just Leopold. I used to cook here.

Silence. Imani lowers her glass. He lifts his, to her.

LEOPOLD (CONT'D)
Good soup. Needs salt.

Imani smiles. She stands, crosses to the stove, adds a pinch. He nods.
